+# Changes
+
+## Round 1
+
+Findings addressed: REVIEW.md (round 0) item 6, the only UNMET item. Items
+1-5 were MET and stay so; item 4 needed the README corrected to match the
+new behaviour, which this round does.
+
+- `src/duration.mjs`: the grammar now accepts every shape REVIEW.md item 6
+  lists as failing, while still refusing every shape it says must keep
+  throwing.
+  - Units match regardless of letter case (regex `i` flag):
+    `"1H30M"` → `5400`, `"500MS"` → `0.5`.
+  - The text is trimmed before matching, so surrounding whitespace is
+    ignored: `"  45s  "` → `45`. A whitespace-only text (`"   "`) trims to
+    the empty string and throws `RangeError`, as before.
+  - `\s*` is allowed between parts: `"1h 30m"` → `5400`. Nothing is allowed
+    between a number and its unit, so `"1 h"` still throws.
+  - Each number may carry a fraction with digits on both sides of the point
+    (`[0-9]+(?:\.[0-9]+)?`): `"1.5h"` → `5400`, `"0.5m"` → `30`,
+    `"0.25h"` → `900`, `"1.5s"` → `1.5`. `".5s"` and `"5.s"` still throw.
+  - Still refused with `RangeError` (checked against the list REVIEW.md
+    quotes): `"1e2s"`, `"-1h"`, `"+1h"`, `"1_000s"`, `"1h,30m"`,
+    `"1h and 30m"`, `"Infinity"`, `"h"`, `"1h30"`, `"30m1h"`, `"1h1h"`,
+    `"1d"`, `""`; `90`, `null`, `["1h"]` still throw `TypeError`.
+    `"5ms"` is still `0.005` and `"1h0m0s"` is still `3600`.
+  - The header comment and JSDoc describe the new grammar (REVIEW.md noted
+    the old comment at `src/duration.mjs:1-4` documented the opposite).
+- `tests/duration.test.mjs`: the tests that asserted the opposite of the
+  held-out expectations (whitespace around and between parts, upper-case
+  units, `"1.5h"`, `"0.5s"`) are replaced by three new tests that assert the
+  accepted shapes (`ignores the letter case of units`, `trims whitespace
+  around the text`, `allows whitespace between parts`, `allows a fraction on
+  any part`), and the refusal tests are regrouped so each shape that must
+  still throw is covered: whitespace-only text and whitespace inside a part
+  (`"   "`, `"1 h"`, non-breaking space), malformed fractions (`".5s"`,
+  `"5.s"`, `"1.h"`, `"1.5.5h"`), signs, exponents and digit separators
+  (`"-1h"`, `"+1h"`, `"1e2s"`, `"1_000s"`), other separators (`"1h,30m"`,
+  `"1h and 30m"`), `"Infinity"`, `"1h30"`, plus `"5ms"` → `0.005` and
+  `"1h0m0s"` → `3600`, and `90` as a non-string `TypeError` case.
+- `README.md`: the `parseDuration` paragraph no longer says parts must be
+  whole ASCII digits with a lowercase unit and no whitespace; it now lists
+  the three relaxations (letter case, whitespace around and between parts
+  but not inside one, fractions with digits on both sides of the point) with
+  examples, and the `RangeError` list no longer names fractions, upper-case
+  units or whitespace as throwing. The `TypeError` sentence gives examples.
+
+`npm test`: 17 tests, 17 pass, 0 fail, 0 skipped, 0 todo, exit 0.
+
+## Round 0
+
+Findings addressed: none yet (first round, no REVIEW.md).
+
+- `src/duration.mjs` (new): exports `parseDuration(text)`, the inverse of
+  `formatSeconds`. A non-string throws `TypeError`. The text must match
+  `^(?:[0-9]+h)?(?:[0-9]+m)?(?:[0-9]+s)?(?:[0-9]+ms)?$` and be non-empty;
+  anything else throws `RangeError`. The sum is taken in whole milliseconds
+  and divided by 1000 once, so `"1m1s"` is exactly `61`.
+- Decisions on the open points, taking the strictest reading consistent with
+  "inverse of formatSeconds" (it only ever writes lowercase units, ASCII
+  integer digits, no separators):
+  - whitespace anywhere (leading, trailing, between parts, inside a part):
+    refused;
+  - upper-case units (`1H`, `500MS`, `500Ms`): refused;
+  - fractions, signs, exponents (`1.5h`, `.5s`, `-1h`, `+1h`, `1e3s`): refused;
+  - no unit (`90`, `1h30`), unknown unit (`1d`, `1hour`), out-of-order or
+    repeated units (`30m1h`, `1h1h`), empty string, separators (`1:30`,
+    `1h,30m`): refused;
+  - non-ASCII digits (`١h`, `１h`) and non-breaking space: refused;
+  - `String` objects, arrays and objects with `toString`: `TypeError`
+    (only primitive strings are accepted);
+  - a digit run of any length is accepted (`0s` is `0`, `100h` is `360000`),
+    and a total that overflows to a non-finite number throws `RangeError`.
+- `tests/duration.test.mjs` (new): covers the task's examples, each unit alone
+  and combined, the round trip `parseDuration(formatSeconds(n))` for `5400`,
+  `61`, `0.5`, `0` and more, and one test per refused shape above.
+- `README.md`: documents `parseDuration` beside `formatSeconds`, with examples
+  and a list of what throws `RangeError` and what throws `TypeError`.
+
+`npm test`: 14 tests, 14 pass, 0 fail, 0 skipped, 0 todo, exit 0.
